# Exclude from the SkyPilot workdir sync (gitignore-style). Managed jobs upload the
# workdir to a GCS bucket, so keep it to *code only*: the VM rebuilds the venv (`uv sync`)
# and fetches data from the DVC remote (`dvc pull`). Shipping .venv/ and data/ is slow,
# symlink-fragile (mmseqs temp dirs), and redundant.
#
# NOTE: this file is NOT .gitignore — SkyPilot only auto-excludes .git, so anything gitignored but
# not listed here still gets uploaded. A 1.6 GB .venv went up that way once, and a 910 MB
# .evodiff_env was mid-upload before being caught. A test now derives the required entries from
# editjumps/**/install_*.sh rather than trusting this list to stay complete, but when you add a large
# local-only directory, add it in BOTH places.
# Sanity check before a managed launch:
#   du -sm * .[!.]* 2>/dev/null | sort -rn | head    # anything big and not listed below?
.venv/
.evodiff_env/
# Agent worktrees: each is a full repo copy, and one carried a 910 MB .evodiff_env — 6.4 GB
# total, which hung two launches for ~50 minutes on the workdir upload before this was added.
# Never needed on the VM: the job re-clones nothing and reads data from the DVC remote.
.claude/
.uvcache_tmp/
.dvc_cache_global/
data/
.dvc/cache/
*.db
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.terraform/
deploy/gcp/terraform/.terraform/
figures/
